--- !u!114 &3712860397859273092
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "The XRI Network Manager prefab is required to be in the Scene\u2019s hierarchy in order to manage all the required network connections between XR Interaction Toolkit (XRI), Netcode for GameObjects (NGO), and Unity Gaming Services (UGS.)\n\n<b>Note:</b> <i>This prefab, or a variant / override of this, must be in your scene</i>.\n\nThe <b>XRI Network Game Manager (Script)</b> component handles the high level connection states, high level joining and leaving rooms, connected player info, and most core connection logic.\n\nThe <b>Lobby Manager (Script)</b> component handles the communication with the Unity Lobby service and Unity Relay service.\n\nThe <b>Authentication Manager (Script)</b> component handles the authentication process to the Unity Services at runtime. This template uses <b>Anonymous sign in</b>, which can be overridden using a sign in provider.\n\nThe Anonymous sign in requires all connected players to have a <b>Unique Sign in</b>. Authentication Manager handles this automatically for ParrelSync and Multiplayer Play Mode, but requires that all tags or arguments are set to unique strings. Additionally, when testing multiple standalone builds on the same machine, you can pass \"PlayerArg:X\" as a command line argument to make sure your sign in profile is unique (make sure X is unique per player instance).\n\nUse the following code anywhere to easily and quickly connect to any available room (or create a new room if none are available):"
--- !u!114 &4953293621724920500
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'The <b>MR Interaction Setup</b> prefab contains the essential XRI components along with the XR Rig and all other required configurations necessary in a Mixed Reality context.


      <b>Note:</b> <i>This prefab, or a variant / override of this, must be in your scene</i>.


      A few <b>important</b> callouts:


      <b>XR Origin (XR Rig)</b>: This contains a slight variant of the rig prefab from the Hand Interaction Demo XRI Sample.


      <b>XR Origin -> Offline Player Avatar</b>: This prefab is a slightly modified version of the player prefab visuals.


      <b>XR Origin -> Local Player Canvas -> Player Notification UI</b>:  This prefab allows you to make very simple notification popup using the follow code (called from anywhere):'
