    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "The <b>Network Manager XR Multiplayer</b> prefab handles the high level connection data used by Netcode for GameObjects (NGO.)\n\n<b>Note:</b> <i>This prefab, or a variant / override of this, must be in your scene</i>.\n\nThe <b>Network Manager XR Multiplayer (Script)</b> component contains a multitude of network properties and options under the <b> Network Config</b> dropdown, which can be edited to accommodate specific needs.\n\nUse the <b>Player Prefab</b> property to set the reference to your player prefab, which is the object that gets instantiated for all connected clients (players.)\n\nUse the <b>Prefabs -> Network Prefabs Lists</b> to set the data reference for any objects that are instantiated at runtime. \n<b>Note:</b> <I>Any object that is spawned on the network during runtime is required to be listed here. Objects that already placed in the scene do not need to be referenced in this list.</i>\n\nTo test Quick Joining during runtime, click the <b>Connect</b> button located at the very bottom of the <b>Network Manager XR Multiplayer (Script)</b> component."
